nts in Study of Quality of Life Among Obese and Normal-Weight Men and Women, Turkey, 2005</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" scope="col" rowspan="3" colspan="1">Survey Item</th><th align="center" scope="col" colspan="2" rowspan="1">Obese</th><th align="center" scope="col" colspan="2" rowspan="1">Normal Weight</th></tr><tr><th colspan="4" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Women (n = 1498)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Men (n = 254)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Women (n = 250)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Men (n = 150)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" scope="col" colspan="5" rowspan="1"><bold>In general, health is</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Excellent</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.0</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10.3</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.4</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">29.8</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Very good</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">11.1</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.6</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30.1</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">34.1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Good</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.7</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15.1</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.7</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20.1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fair</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20.7</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">29.9</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10.1</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.6</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Po